WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.060
But anyway, the federal government . . . We have the Endangered Species Act,

2
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.820
which was passed in the early ’70s and the sea turtle population was crashing.

3
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:17.220
The nesting turtles in Mexico and Texas was just going down drastically.

4
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.460
Anyway to make a long story short,

5
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:26.240
they passed a federal law that said that all the shrimpers in Louisiana and the Gulf Coast had to pull all these turtle excluder devices.

6
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.800
And there was shrimp loss involved.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.980
So the day . . . it was supposed to go into effect on a Monday.

8
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:40.720
On Saturday morning, I get a call from state representative Randy Roach, who’s now mayor of Lake Charles by the way.

9
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.280
He called me and said, “Paul, what are you doing?”

10
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.280
I said, “Nothing, I’m just getting ready to go do some work outside.”

11
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.347
He said, “You need to meet me in Cameron.

12
00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.680
We got a problem.”

13
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.893
The shrimpers had blocked the ship channel in Cameron.

14
00:00:51.893 --> 00:00:56.980
Now blocking a federal ship channel is an act of war.

15
00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.360
So I said, “What do you think we’re going to do?”

16
00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.320
He said, “I don’t know, but let’s go.”

17
00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.180
So we met.

18
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.100
We might have met in Creole and then we drove together.

19
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:11.140
But when I got there, it was just scary because these shrimpers had blocked the channel.

20
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.660
There was a recreational fishing rodeo going on from Lake Charles.

21
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:20.960
They weren’t letting the boats back in, let alone boats that were going offshore back into Lake Charles.

22
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.760
The wives were all gathered on the shore.

23
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.760
They all came running, “Mr. Paul, Mr. Paul, you got to do something.

24
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.480
Get on the radio and talk to them.”

25
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.160
And they had these VHF radios.

26
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.720
So I got on the radio and asked them, “What are y’all going to do?”

27
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:39.200
“Well, we’re not buckling ’til they say this rule’s not going to be implemented.”

28
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.900
Seventeen hours of negotiations Randy and I did.

29
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:50.020
They were shuttling beer to these fishermen, we heard shots fired in the air.

30
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.140
You know there were some guns.

31
00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.860
No one was shot, but they had guns.

32
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.920
It’s something that I hoped to never to have to do again.

33
00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.380
We talked to them and we did get the congress . . . In fact,

34
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:10.360
we had our congressman on the phone during the negotiations and he was talking to the national fisheries services.

35
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.660
They agreed to delay it for two weeks or something.

36
00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:20.960
I think it was a week or two weeks, and they actually decided to go on and open up the blockade.

37
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.560
When we got there the Coast Guard had been called and they were just getting there.

38
00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.260
And realize that the Coast Guard is eighteen, nineteen, twenty year old people.

39
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:34.640
They were spraying water cannons through the windshields of the shrimp boats trying to get them to break up.

40
00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:41.940
Randy calls the governor’s office, which was Governor [Buddy] Roemer, and he asked Roemer, “Pull them back.

41
00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.580
Get the Coast Guard back.”

42
00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:53.020
So, they pulled back and went back to Lake Charles because we would have had some people hurt.

43
00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:59.560
Probably the most scary and real life experience of potential violence that I’ve ever seen.
